credentials/

# THE TEMPLATE, RE-INCLUDED HERE AND NOT ONLY AT THE ROOT.
#
# The root file excludes `**/.env.*` and re-includes `!**/.env.example`. That is
# correct and it depends on how a particular git reads `**` inside a negation —
# a CI runner disagreed with a laptop about it, and reported this file as
# ignored. A deeper .gitignore takes precedence over a shallower one on every
# version, so saying it again here settles the question rather than relying on
# the two agreeing.
!.env.example
